    "status": "live",
    "notes": "The Pacific Northwest's loud station: grunge (playtest 2, 2026-10-02: \"There should be different stations and music in different regions\"). Since playtest 4 (P4-17: \"PNW seems very simple and slow\") each track is a whole sixteen-bar song at 112-148 bpm: a drop-tuned riff, a quiet verse of clean arpeggios, a build, a loud chorus of chugged power chords whose hook returns with a harmony, and the riff to close (src/audio/radio-compose-pnw.ts, preset grunge-band). It played slow surf before playtest 2; the song names stayed. Melodies are generated from each track's seed, so they are original. Cut a track by setting its status to vetoed.",
